Getting the help in databricks CLI
databricks secrets -h

Step1: Creating Profile for the Databricks workspace
databricks configure --profile <new_profile_name>

Step 2: Create scope inside the profile (scope is a placeholder where you create different keys)

List existing scops using profile 
databricks secrets list-scopes --profile <new_profile_name>

Create New scope inside the profile
databricks secrets create-scope --scope storage --profile cns_ibm_dev

Step 3: Creating new Secret inside the scope
databricks secrets put-secret storage cnsibmdevsp --profile cns_ibm_dev

Note: To change the key for the same secrete, run the same command then the Notepad will open, where we need to place the secrete for the scope 

List existing secrets inside the scope
databricks secrets list-secrets <scope_name> --profile <profile_name>

To check the secrets inside a particular scope, use: This can be done only through DBX as below
value=dbutils.secrets.get("<scope name>","<secret name>")
for i in value:
    print(i,end=' ')
